{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: siwa-button | Owner: A-02 | Task: ST-03

  A-01 Button. Every committed action in the store comes through here, so the
  hierarchy between two actions is decided by a parameter and not by whoever
  happened to write the markup that day.

  THE LABEL IS THE CALLER'S, ALREADY TRANSLATED.
  A snippet cannot know whether its label is a locale key, a schema setting or
  a string built from a price, so it does not guess: the caller resolves the
  copy and hands over the finished text. `label` blank renders NOTHING — a
  control with no accessible name is worse than a missing control, and an
  empty <button> would be a rule-10 error the moment it shipped.

  GOLD IS RATIONED BY THE CALLER, NOT HERE.
  Principle 1 allows one --primary per fold. This snippet will render as many
  as it is asked to; deciding that a surface has already spent its gold is the
  calling section's job, and CI warning 14 counts them per section.

  Principle 7: the tester is a first-class CTA and takes the outline
  treatment. --tester and --secondary are visually identical on purpose, and
  they are separate classes so that a rule can assert the tester was never
  rendered as --primary on a surface that carries another CTA. Never pass
  variant: 'primary' for a tester unless it is the only CTA on the surface.

  NO BEHAVIOUR. The behaviour layer is assets/siwa-theme.js; a caller wires it
  by handing over the hook attributes through `data_attrs`.

  Parameters
    label       required. Already-translated string. Blank renders nothing.
    href        optional. Present renders <a>, absent renders <button type="button">.
    variant     optional. primary | secondary | tester | quiet | text. Default secondary.
    size        optional. 'sm' adds --sm; the visual box drops to 40px and the
                CSS extends the hit area back to 44px. Anything else is default.
    block       optional boolean. Adds --block for full-width in cart and on mobile.
    aria_label  optional. Overrides the visible label as the accessible name.
                Required by rule 10 for any control whose label is an icon.
    data_attrs  optional. Raw attribute string, for the behaviour layer's hooks.
    id          optional. DOM id, for aria-controls and label associations.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign button_variant = variant | default: 'secondary'
  assign button_class = 'siwa-button siwa-button--' | append: button_variant

  if size == 'sm'
    assign button_class = button_class | append: ' siwa-button--sm'
  endif

  if block
    assign button_class = button_class | append: ' siwa-button--block'
  endif
-%}

{%- if label != blank -%}
  {%- if href != blank -%}
    <a
      class="{{ button_class }}"
      href="{{ href }}"
      {%- if id != blank %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}
      {%- if aria_label != blank %} aria-label="{{ aria_label | escape }}"{% endif %}
      {{ data_attrs }}
    >{{ label }}</a>
  {%- else -%}
    <button
      class="{{ button_class }}"
      type="button"
      {%- if id != blank %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}
      {%- if aria_label != blank %} aria-label="{{ aria_label | escape }}"{% endif %}
      {{ data_attrs }}
    >{{ label }}</button>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
